From da6d49e5a5331dc472ffb7593c7a0e5bddb27510 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:50:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: map the OUTPUT buffers read-write too

The v10 decoder firmware writes to the stream buffers it reads, using
the coded picture buffer as work space. An imported dmabuf queued on
the OUTPUT queue is mapped DMA_TO_DEVICE, read-only in the IOMMU, and
on Exynos7870 the write is a System MMU access protection fault, which
panics. It showed with a 720x1278 H.264 stream; 1080p streams played
without it.

Make the OUTPUT queues bidirectional, as the CAPTURE ones already are.

---
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
index 7899a8140d..bb342200c2 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
@@ -964,6 +964,12 @@ static int s5p_mfc_open(struct file *file)
 		ret = -ENOENT;
 		goto err_queue_init;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * The v10 firmware also writes to the stream buffers it reads (the
+	 * decoder uses the CPB as work space): an imported dmabuf mapped
+	 * DMA_TO_DEVICE is read-only in the IOMMU, and the write faults.
+	 */
+	q->bidirectional = 1;
 	/* One way to indicate end-of-stream for MFC is to set the
 	 * bytesused == 0. However by default videobuf2 handles bytesused
 	 * equal to 0 as a special case and changes its value to the size
-- 
